    "summary": "Map of Northern Persia; single-page drawing on an album folio. Detailed map includes Isfahan, Ardabil and Astarabad, along with various other towns, travel routes, and natural topography (mountains, seas, rivers). Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
